+## Part of the Ashlr ecosystem
+
+Stack is one tool in the Ashlr ecosystem. Together these tools aim to be an autonomous, code-first, agent-native software factory, chasing open-source RSI (recursive self-improvement). Agents do the work, and the human acts as a passive board member. Stack is the service layer: it turns provider setup into commands an agent can run and parse.
+
+- Phantom (`@ashlr/phantom`, command `phm`): runs the agents that improve these repos, for example `phm improve`.
+- Phantom Secrets (`phantom`): the vault. Stack stores the secrets you select here. https://github.com/ashlrai/phantom-secrets
+- Locus (`locus`): identity plane. Pins which account a session acts as; `stack exec --as` uses it. https://github.com/ashlrai/locus
+- Lexicon (`lexicon`): voice lexicon. Keeps dictated names spelled right. https://github.com/ashlrai/lexicon
+- Ashlr Markdown (`mdopener-mcp`): desktop Markdown app with an MCP server. https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-md
+- Ashlr plugin (`ashlr-plugin`): plugin for Claude Code and Codex. https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-plugin
+- Ashlr Stack (`stack`): configures services and wires them into agents. https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-stack
+
+`stack doctor --ecosystem --json` reports which of these are installed, with versions. It is read-only. `stack doctor --ecosystem --install` prints install commands for missing tools and runs nothing.
+
+Agents also work on the Stack repo itself: Phantom and other coding agents open branches and pull requests and merge them once required checks pass. Their rules and kept limits (secrets, billing, force-push) are in https://github.com/ashlrai/ashlr-stack/blob/main/AGENTS.md.
